            "date": "2026-10-09T08:21:21+02:00"
          },
          "message": "chore: migrate fetch and htmx modules to Typescript (#14705)\n\nThis PR converts our `fetch.js` module and HTMX configurator to Typescript, adding appropriate types along the way. This continues the work from !14508, a scoped approach to tightening our frontend type-checking, in line with @JakobDev's assessment in https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/5859#issuecomment-2560264.\n\nI also changed one instance of `innerHTML = ''` to assign `textContent` instead. We only ever set it to an empty string here, which is safe enough, but `textContent` never bothers about any HTML parsing machinery, and it's good practice to avoid directly assigning `innerHTML` wherever possible. This is also in line with [MDN's recommendation](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/API/Node/textContent#differences_from_innerhtml) on the subject.\n\nUnfortunately, adding these types altered enough lines that Git doesn't see `fetch.ts` as a file rename, which would affect the blame readout. I'm not sure there's a good way around that.\n\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/14705\nReviewed-by: Gusted <redacted@example.invalid>\n",
          "tree": {
            "url": "https://codeberg.org/api/v1/repos/forgejo/forgejo/git/trees/3a7f257f531ea2e4bc74532ebc9c37d0bb966217",
            "sha": "3a7f257f531ea2e4bc74532ebc9c37d0bb966217",
